Description: Resolve CLI forwarding paths from the versioned SDK directory
Author: Chet Husk <chethusk@microsoft.com>, copilot-swe-agent[bot]
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/55988
Bug: https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/issues/55919
Bug: https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/issues/56244
Applied-Upstream: 11.0.100-rc.2, https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/commit/9489ae1dd6b9e2b2f357974b3a4cb905272422d2
Last-Update: 2026-09-18
---
Since .NET 11 the CLI ships a Native AOT front end (libdotnet-aot.so, built on
amd64 and arm64) that the muxer loads directly instead of going through
hostfxr.  Inside that native bubble nothing sets APP_CONTEXT_BASE_DIRECTORY, so
AppContext.BaseDirectory resolves to the install root (/usr/lib/dotnet) rather
than the versioned SDK directory (/usr/lib/dotnet/sdk/<version>).  See
src/sdk/src/Cli/dotnet-aot/SdkRootResolution.md.

Five call sites still derived SDK-relative paths from AppContext.BaseDirectory
and therefore looked for their payload one directory tree too high:

  dotnet format  -> /usr/lib/dotnet/DotnetTools/dotnet-format/dotnet-format.dll
  dotnet nuget   -> /usr/lib/dotnet/NuGet.CommandLine.XPlat.dll
  dotnet vstest  -> /usr/lib/dotnet/vstest.console.dll
  dotnet fsi     -> /usr/lib/dotnet/FSharp/fsi.dll
  external command search (EnvironmentProvider) probed the install root

"dotnet format" failed outright with "The application to execute does not
exist", which the bundled-tools-can-execute autopkgtest catches.  The other
four are the same defect and fail the same way once reached.

Use SdkPaths.SdkDirectory, which prefers the Microsoft.DotNet.Sdk.Root
AppContext value published by the AOT bridge and stays equivalent to
AppContext.BaseDirectory for the managed CLI.  Microsoft.DotNet.Cli.CoreUtils
already grants InternalsVisibleTo to dotnet, dotnet-aot and
Microsoft.DotNet.Cli.Utils, so no project changes are needed.

Only the product sources from the upstream backport are carried here; its new
test/dotnet-aot.Tests/ files are omitted because the SDK unit tests are not
built during the Debian build, and the accompanying
test/dotnet-aot.Tests/MSBuildEvaluationTests.cs hunk only removes a helper that
those new files replace.

This patch can be dropped once the package is rebased onto 11.0.100-rc.2 or
later.

